                                "sense_id": "a5d26d98-0d7a-3a94-ad93-27e612e610a9",
                                "text": "The tortoise—as the alderman of Bristol, well learned in eating, knows by much experience—besides the delicious calipash and calipee, contains many different kinds of food."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fe4b6f4-aea3-4ff2-ad74-165f8a00bc77",
                                "sense_id": "a5d26d98-0d7a-3a94-ad93-27e612e610a9",
                                "text": "Dobbin helped him to it; for the lady of the house, before whom the tureen was placed, was so ignorant of the contents that she was going to help Mr. Sedley without bestowing upon him either calipash or calipee."
                            }
